  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Khao pad serves 2 and takes about 15 minutes. The secret is day-old "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "jasmine rice",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "jasmine-rice"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Freshly cooked rice is too wet and will steam rather than fry. Cold refrigerated rice breaks apart cleanly in the hot wok and fries to a light, fluffy texture."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use the highest heat your hob can produce. Fried rice needs to move quickly or it clumps. Have everything prepped and within arm's reach before you start."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 2,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "jasmine-rice",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cooked and cold, ideally day-old",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "eggs",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "beaten",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "garlic",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "cloves",
              "prepNote": "finely chopped",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "spring-onion",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "sliced, white and green parts separated",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "fish-sauce",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "soy-sauce-light",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 0.5,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lime",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "cut into wedges to serve",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a wok over high heat until smoking. Add the garlic and white parts of the spring onions. Stir for 30 seconds."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the cold rice. Press it flat against the wok and let it sit for 30 seconds. Break it up and toss. Repeat to get some light colour on the grains."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Push the rice to one side. Pour the beaten eggs into the cleared space. Scramble briefly, then fold through the rice before fully set."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add {{fish-sauce}}, {{soy-sauce-light}}, and {{caster-sugar}}. Toss everything together."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the green parts of the spring onions. Toss once more and remove from the heat."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Serve with lime wedges on the side. Squeeze over just before eating."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Rice is clumping into wet lumps",
              "cause": "Rice was freshly cooked or still warm",
              "fix": "Always use cold, day-old rice. Spread it on a tray to dry further if needed."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Egg is rubbery and overcooked",
              "cause": "Egg was scrambled too long before folding in",
              "fix": "Fold the egg in while it is still slightly wet. The rice carries enough heat to finish it."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Rice has no colour or flavour",
              "cause": "Not enough heat or too much rice for the wok",
              "fix": "Cook in a single portion at a time. A crowded wok steams the rice instead of frying it."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Khao pad means fried rice in Thai. It is the original leftover meal and appears in some form at almost every Thai meal time. The base is always jasmine rice fried with egg, garlic, and spring onions. From there, cooks add whatever is available: chicken, prawns, pork, or just vegetables. It is sold at street stalls for a few baht and cooked at home almost daily. The lime wedge served alongside is not decoration. It brightens the whole dish."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
